From: Camera firmware maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] simple-protocol: enforce existing client limit and bound accept logs

The simple protocol defines CLIENTS_MAX but did not enforce it. Close
newly accepted sockets at the limit before allocating a Client. Avoid
unbounded error logging when accept fails from descriptor exhaustion.
Other accept errors retain the existing logging.

This is a narrow local resource bound inspired by the client admission
and error handling in upstream proposal 808. It intentionally does not
port the unmerged credential/rlimit refactor. An attacker holding all
slots can still deny new simple-protocol clients. Accept readiness after
EMFILE/ENFILE can still consume CPU because no listener backoff is added.
This mitigates daemon memory, descriptor and error-log exhaustion.

Related candidate: CVE-2025-59529 (partial resource mitigation only)
Upstream-Status: Pending [https://github.com/avahi/avahi/pull/808]

--- a/avahi-daemon/simple-protocol.c
+++ b/avahi-daemon/simple-protocol.c
@@ -443,8 +443,12 @@
     if (events & AVAHI_WATCH_IN) {
         int cfd;
 
-        if ((cfd = accept(fd, NULL, NULL)) < 0)
-            avahi_log_error("accept(): %s", strerror(errno));
+        if ((cfd = accept(fd, NULL, NULL)) < 0) {
+            /* Do not let descriptor exhaustion flood the error log. */
+            if (errno != EMFILE && errno != ENFILE)
+                avahi_log_error("accept(): %s", strerror(errno));
+        } else if (s->n_clients >= CLIENTS_MAX)
+            close(cfd);
         else
             client_new(s, cfd);
     }
